fers the lottery that is more left-skewed' where 'left-skewed' is defined as having more probability on favorable outcomes. This is a mislabeling, but we proceed with the given definition. Under this misdefinition, Lottery B (100% chance of 2000 Euros) has all probability on favorable outcomes, so it is more 'left-skewed' under the given definition. Lottery A is symmetric, so it has equal probability on favorable and unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, under this reason, B is preferred. The information relevant to the decision reason is thus available: we can determine the skewness under the given (incorrect) definition.",
